-- url     : https://prove2.me/theorems/4664b871-8a59-5d62-8d48-9c23abfd306e
-- title:
--   Every rational place is read at a closed special point
-- statement:
--   Throughout, $q$ is a prime with $5 \le q$, $M'$ is a nonzero natural number with $q \nmid M'$, and $A$ is a valuation subring of $\overline{\mathbb Q} =$ `AlgebraicClosure ℚ` with `A.LiesOverPrime q`, i.e. $q$ is a nonunit of $A$. Here `modularFunctionFieldBar M'` is the base change to $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ (`laurentBaseChange`) of `modularFunctionFieldFull M'` inside Laurent series, `fieldBar q M'` is `xHFunctionFieldBar (q ^ 2 * M') (levelH q M')`, where `levelH q M'` is the kernel of the unit-group reduction map attached to the divisibility `dvd_sq_mul q M'`, and `modularFunctionFieldC K M'`, `xHFunctionFieldC K (q ^ 2 * M') (levelH q M')` are the corresponding $q$-expansion fields over a field $K$. A `Place K F` is a valuation subring of $F$ containing $K$, different from $F$, whose ideals are principal; it is rational (`IsRational`) when $K$ maps onto its residue field, `evalAt` is the resulting $K$-valued evaluation, and `ord` is minus the logarithm of the attached $\mathbb{Z}^{m0}$-valued adic valuation.
--
--   **Data on the special fibre.** $W$ is a finite set of places of `modularFunctionFieldC (ResidueField A) M'` over `ResidueField A`, and the hypothesis `hW` says that $W$ consists exactly of the supersingular places `ssPlaces q M' (ResidueField A)`: those rational places $w$ that are affine geometric places with $w.\mathrm{evalAt}$ of the generator `jGeomGen` lying in `ssJSet q (ResidueField A)`, the set of $j$-values all of whose elliptic curves have no nonzero $q$-torsion. The hypothesis `hle` is the inclusion `modularFunctionFieldBar M' ≤ fieldBar q M'`. Next, $R_0$ is a `ConstantReduction` of $A$ from `modularFunctionFieldBar M'` to `modularFunctionFieldC (ResidueField A) M'`: a valuation subring `R₀.integers`, a surjective ring map `R₀.residue` to the target with kernel the maximal ideal, contracting to $A$ along the structure map and inducing `IsLocalRing.residue` on $A$, together with the scaling property `exists_smul_mem` and a map `placeMap` on places preserving degrees and compatible with divisors of nonzero residues. The hypothesis `hR₀` says that for every Laurent series $y$ over $A$ whose image in Laurent series over $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ lies in `modularFunctionFieldBar M'`, that image lies in `R₀.integers` and its $R_0$-residue is, as a Laurent series over `ResidueField A`, the coefficientwise reduction of $y$.
--
--   **Branch and supersingular valuation rings.** $\zeta$ is an element of `Idx q`, i.e. a primitive $q$-th root of unity in $\overline{\mathbb Q}$; `levelAutBar q M' ζ' γ` denotes the $\overline{\mathbb Q}$-automorphism of `fieldBar q M'` selected by the predicate `IsLevelAutBar` (the identity if none exists), and `redQ q` is reduction $\mathrm{SL}_2(\mathbb Z) \to \mathrm{GL}_2(\mathbb Z/q)$ acting on [`CuspidalType.ProjLine q`](def/CuspidalType_IsCuspidalOfType.html#L21), with `lineInfty q` the point $[1:0]$. Two families of valuation subrings of `fieldBar q M'` are given: $O_{\mathrm{Ig}}$ indexed by `ProjLine q` and $O_{\mathrm{SS}}$ indexed by $W$. The Igusa group of hypotheses consists of: `hIg_inf`, which characterises $O_{\mathrm{Ig}}(\mathrm{lineInfty}\,q)$ as the set of $f$ for which there are Laurent series $x,y$ over $A$ with $y$ not reducing to $0$ and $f\cdot y = x$ after coefficientwise inclusion $A \subseteq \overline{\mathbb Q}$; `hIg`, that every line $\ell$ is $\mathrm{redQ}\,q\,\gamma \cdot \mathrm{lineInfty}\,q$ for some $\gamma \in \Gamma_0(M')$ with $O_{\mathrm{Ig}}(\ell)$ the pullback of $O_{\mathrm{Ig}}(\mathrm{lineInfty}\,q)$ along `levelAutBar q M' ζ γ`; `hIg_inj`, injectivity of $O_{\mathrm{Ig}}$; and `hIg_perm`, that for each $\zeta'$ and each $\gamma \in \Gamma_0(M')$ the pullbacks along `levelAutBar q M' ζ' γ` permute the family $O_{\mathrm{Ig}}$. The supersingular group consists of: `hSS_A`, that an element of $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ lies in $O_{\mathrm{SS}}(s)$ exactly when it lies in $A$; `hSS_over`, that for $s \in W$ and $f \in R_0.\mathrm{integers}$ whose order is nonnegative at every place of `modularFunctionFieldBar M'` over $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ at which the $j$-expansion `coeffEmb (AlgebraicClosure ℚ) jq` has nonnegative order, and whose $R_0$-residue lies in the valuation subring of $s$, the image of $f$ in `fieldBar q M'` lies in $O_{\mathrm{SS}}(s)$, and moreover for every $a \in A$ with `residue A a` equal to $s.\mathrm{evalAt}$ of that residue the difference of the image of $f$ and $a$ lies in the maximal ideal of $O_{\mathrm{SS}}(s)$; `hSS_fix`, that each $O_{\mathrm{SS}}(s)$ is invariant under pullback along every `levelAutBar q M' ζ' γ` with $\gamma \in \Gamma_0(M')$; and `hSS_tr`, that each $O_{\mathrm{SS}}(s)$ contains an element $t$ such that $t - a$ is a unit of $O_{\mathrm{SS}}(s)$ for every $a \in A$.
--
--   **Prolongation.** $R$ is a `RegularProlongation` of $A$ from `fieldBar q M'` to `xHFunctionFieldC (ResidueField A) (q ^ 2 * M') (levelH q M')` (the same data as a `ConstantReduction` without `placeMap` and its two compatibilities), with `hR` asserting `R.integers = OIg (lineInfty q)`, and `hR₀O` asserting that $f \in R_0.\mathrm{integers}$ holds exactly when the image of $f$ in `fieldBar q M'` lies in $O_{\mathrm{Ig}}(\mathrm{lineInfty}\,q)$.
--
--   **Arithmetic of the base.** An element $\pi \in \overline{\mathbb Q}$ is given with $\pi^{q^2-1} = q$ and $\pi \in A$. A subfield $k_0 \subseteq \overline{\mathbb Q}$ over $\mathbb Q$ is given together with $\pi_0 \in k_0$ lying in $A$ such that the contraction $A \cap k_0$ is a discrete valuation ring with maximal ideal generated by $\pi_0$, is henselian local, and has algebraically closed residue field (`hdvr`, `hunif`, `hhens`, `hres`), and `hκ` requires every $a \in A$ to be congruent modulo the maximal ideal of $A$ to some element of $k_0$ lying in $A$. An auxiliary prime $\ell$ is given with $3 \le \ell$, $\ell \ne q$, $\ell \nmid M'$, an element $\zeta_0 \in k_0$ that is a primitive $q\ell$-th root of unity in $\overline{\mathbb Q}$, and an element $\varpi_t \in k_0$ lying in $A$ with $\varpi_t^{q^2-1} = q\,u$ for some unit $u$ of $A$. Finally $K_1$ is a finite extension of $k_0$ inside $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ and $A_1$ a valuation subring of $K_1$ with $x \in A_1$ exactly when $x \in A$, assumed to be a henselian discrete valuation ring.
--
--   **Conclusion.** With `fieldBar q M'` regarded as a $k_0$-algebra through $\overline{\mathbb Q}$, the assertion is the following, for every intermediate field $F_0$ of `fieldBar q M'` over $k_0$ subject to four conditions: the compositum of $F_0$ with the $k_0$-subfield generated by the image of $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ is all of `fieldBar q M'`; $F_0$ is stable under every `levelAutBar q M' ζ' γ` with $\gamma \in \Gamma_0(M')$; a linear disjointness condition, namely that for every finite extension $K'$ of $k_0$ in $\overline{\mathbb Q}$, every $m$, every $c : \mathrm{Fin}\,m \to \overline{\mathbb Q}$ linearly independent over $K'$ and every $a : \mathrm{Fin}\,m \to$ `fieldBar q M'` with all $a_i$ in the compositum of $F_0$ with the $k_0$-subfield generated by the image of $K'$, the relation $\sum_i c_i a_i = 0$ forces all $a_i = 0$; and that every element of `fieldBar q M'` whose underlying Laurent series lies in the range of `coeffEmb (AlgebraicClosure ℚ)` belongs to $F_0$.
--
--   Write $T_1$ for the compositum of $F_0$ with the $k_0$-subfield of `fieldBar q M'` generated by the image of $K_1$. Then, for every $A_1$-algebra structure on $T_1$ whose structure map is compatible with the inclusions (the image in `fieldBar q M'` of $a \in A_1$ is the image of $a$ under $K_1 \subseteq \overline{\mathbb Q} \to$ `fieldBar q M'`), for every $j_1 \in T_1$ whose image in `fieldBar q M'` is the image under `IntermediateField.inclusion hle` of the $j$-expansion `coeffEmb (AlgebraicClosure ℚ) jq`, with $j_1 \ne 0$, and for every finite set $N_{\mathrm{Ig}}$ of places of `xHFunctionFieldC (ResidueField A) (q ^ 2 * M') (levelH q M')` for which there exists a ring homomorphism $j$ from `modularFunctionFieldC (ResidueField A) M'` to that field such that, first, for every $f \in R_0.\mathrm{integers}$ the image of $f$ in `fieldBar q M'` lies in `R.integers` with `R.residue` of it equal to $j$ of `R₀.residue` of $f$, and second, $Q \in N_{\mathrm{Ig}}$ holds exactly when there is $s \in W$ with $g$ in the valuation subring of $s$ if and only if $j(g)$ is in the valuation subring of $Q$, for all $g$ — the following holds.
--
--   Let $\mathfrak X =$ [`AlgebraicCurve.TwoChartIntegralModel A₁ T₁ j₁`](def/AlgebraicCurve_TwoChartIntegralModel.html#L236), the pushout glueing $X_{\mathrm{Fin}} = \operatorname{Spec}$ `chartAlgFin` and $X_{\mathrm{Inf}} = \operatorname{Spec}$ `chartAlgInf`, where `chartAlgFin` (resp. `chartAlgInf`) is the subalgebra of elements of $T_1$ integral over $A_1[j_1]$ (resp. over $A_1[j_1^{-1}]$), with `toBase` to $\operatorname{Spec} A_1$ and the canonical morphisms `ιFin`, `ιInf`. Three auxiliary predicates on points $x$ of $\mathfrak X$ and elements $f$ of $T_1$ are used: `InStalk x f` says that for every point $y$ of $X_{\mathrm{Fin}}$ with `ιFin` mapping $y$ to $x$ there are $g,h$ in `chartAlgFin` with $h \notin y.\mathrm{asIdeal}$ and $f h = g$ in $T_1$, and likewise for $X_{\mathrm{Inf}}$ with `chartAlgInf`; `InMax x f` is the same with the additional requirement $g \in y.\mathrm{asIdeal}$; and `Reads x Q` says that every $f$ with `InStalk x f` has its image in `fieldBar q M'` inside `R.integers`, with `R.residue` of it in the valuation subring of $Q$, and `R.residue` of it a nonunit there if and only if `InMax x f` holds.
--
--   The assertion is: for every place $Q$ of `xHFunctionFieldC (ResidueField A) (q ^ 2 * M') (levelH q M')` over `ResidueField A` that is rational, there exists a point $x$ of $\mathfrak X$ such that (i) `toBase` sends $x$ to the closed point of $\operatorname{Spec} A_1$; (ii) $x$ is closed, in the sense that every $y$ with $x \rightsquigarrow y$ equals $x$; (iii) for every $y$ of $X_{\mathrm{Fin}}$ above $x$, every $b$ in `chartAlgFin` whose image in `fieldBar q M'` is a nonunit of `R.integers` lies in $y.\mathrm{asIdeal}$; (iv) the same statement for $X_{\mathrm{Inf}}$ and `chartAlgInf`; and (v) `Reads x Q`.
--
--   Three further abbreviations are introduced alongside: `Centred P x`, asserting that a place $P$ of `fieldBar q M'` over $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ is rational and that every $f$ with `InStalk x f` lies in the valuation subring of $P$ with $P.\mathrm{evalAt}\,f \in A$ and with $A$-valuation less than $1$ exactly when `InMax x f`; `GoodPt x`, the conjunction of clauses (i)–(iv) above together with the requirement that for every $y$ of $X_{\mathrm{Fin}}$ above $x$, every algebraically closed field $\Omega$ of characteristic $q$ and every ring homomorphism $\varphi$ from `chartAlgFin` to $\Omega$ with kernel $y.\mathrm{asIdeal}$, the element $\varphi(\mathrm{jChartFin})$ does not lie in [`ModularCurve.ssJSet q Ω`](def/ModularCurve_SupersingularModuli.html#L7); and `OffBranch x`, asserting that for every line $\ell \ne \mathrm{lineInfty}\,q$ and every $y$ of $X_{\mathrm{Fin}}$ (resp. $X_{\mathrm{Inf}}$) above $x$ there is $b$ in the corresponding chart algebra whose image in `fieldBar q M'` is a nonunit of $O_{\mathrm{Ig}}(\ell)$ and with $b \notin y.\mathrm{asIdeal}$. The conclusion spells out the first four clauses of `GoodPt` and adds `Reads x Q`; its supersingularity clause, as well as `Centred` and `OffBranch`, do not occur in the conclusion.
--
--   This is the existence half of the centring ("reading") step for the two-chart integral model of the full-level modular function field over a henselian discrete valuation ring: each rational place of the Igusa reduced field is realised at a closed point of the special fibre lying on the $\infty$-Igusa chart. It rests on properness of the structure morphism ([`ModularCurve.FullLevel.isProper_toBase_twoChartIntegralModel_levelField`](thm.html#ModularCurve.FullLevel.isProper_toBase_twoChartIntegralModel_levelField)) and is used by [`ModularCurve.FullLevel.exists_goodPt_and_offBranch_and_reads_of_not_mem_igusaNodes_twoChartIntegralModel`](thm.html#ModularCurve.FullLevel.exists_goodPt_and_offBranch_and_reads_of_not_mem_igusaNodes_twoChartIntegralModel), which combines it with the off-branch and non-supersingularity conditions.
